  "title": "79: al-Naazea'at النازعات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنّٰزِعٰتِ غَرْقًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALNNAAZEA’AATE GHARQAN.\nBy those who drag forth violently\nوَّالنّٰشِطٰتِ نَشْطًا ۙ‏(2)\nWWAALNNAASHETAATE NASHTAN.\nAnd those who untie (the knot) briskly\nوَّالسّٰبِحٰتِ سَبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\nWWAALSSAABEHAATE SABHAN.\nAnd those who glide on (Swiftly)\nفَالسّٰبِقٰتِ سَبْقًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAALSSAABEQAATE SABQAN.\nThen those who go ahead with a foremost speed\nفَالْمُدَبِّرٰتِ اَمْرًا‌ ۘ‏(5)\nFAL MUDABBERAATE AMRAN.\nThen those who (submissively) manage the affairs\nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الرَّاجِفَةُ ۙ‏(6)\nYAWMA TARJOFUL AR-RAAJEFATU.\nOn the day on which shall quake the quaking\nتَتْبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُ ؕ‏(7)\nTATBAU’UHAA AR-RAADEFATU.\nShall follow it the quake (by the second trumpet) which shall follow\nقُلُوْبٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّاجِفَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\nQULOOBUN YAWMA-EZIN WWAAJEFATUN.\nHearts that day shall palpitate\nاَبْصَارُهَا خَاشِعَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(9)\nAABSAARUHAA KHAASHE-A’TUN.\nTheir eyes shall be cast down\nيَقُوْلُوْنَ ءَاِنَّا لَمَرْدُوْدُوْنَ فِى الْحَافِرَةِ ؕ‏(10)\nYAQOOLOONA A-INNAA LAMARDOODOONA FIL AL-HAAFERATE.\nThey shall say (then): ‘‘What! Shall we indeed be restored to as (we were) at first?\nءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا نَّخِرَةً ؕ‏(11)\nA-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN NNAKHERATAN.\nWhat! When we are (even) bones rotten?\nقَالُوْا تِلْكَ اِذًا كَرَّةٌ خَاسِرَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\nQAALOO TILKA EZAL KARRATUN KHAASERATUN.\nThey said: ‘‘That then will be a return in vain\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\nFA-INNAMAA HEYA ZAJRATUN WWAAHEDATUN.\nVerily, it shall be but a single (violent) blast\nفَاِذَا هُمْ بِالسَّاهِرَةِ ؕ‏(14)\nFA-EZAA HUM BEALSSAAHERATE.\nWhen lo! they shall (all) be in the awakened state\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(15)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL MOOSAA.\nHath not come unto thee the story of Moses?\nاِذْ نَادٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى‌ۚ‏(16)\nIZ NAADAAHU RABBOHU BIL-WAADE AL-MUQADDASE TOOAA.\nWhen called him his Lord in the Holy Valley (called) ‘Tuva\nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى ۖ‏(17)\nIZHAB ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\n(Saying)-. ‘‘Go thou (O’ Moses!) unto Pharaoh! verily, he hath transgressed the bounds!\nفَقُلْ هَلْ لَّكَ اِلٰٓى اَنْ تَزَكّٰى ۙ‏(18)\nFAQUL HAL LAKA ELAA AN TAZAKKAA.\nAnd say (unto him)’. ‘‘Hast thou (a desire) to cleanse thyself (of thy disbelief)?\nوَاَهْدِيَكَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَتَخْشٰى‌ۚ‏(19)\nWAAHDEEKA ELAA RABBEKA FATAKHSHAA.\nAnd I will guide thee unto thy Lord so that thou mayest fear him\nفَاَرٰٮهُ الْاٰيَةَ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(20)\nFAARAAHU AL-AAAYATA KUBRAA.\nAnd he showed him the greatest sign (miracle)\nفَكَذَّبَ وَعَصٰى ۖ‏(21)\nFA KAZZABA WAA’ASAA.\nBut belied he and disobeyed\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ يَسْعٰىۖ‏(22)\nSUMMA AADBARA YAS-A’A.\nThen turned he his back hastily\nفَحَشَرَ فَنَادٰىۖ‏(23)\nFAHASHARA FANAADAA.\nAnd gathered (the people) and proclaimed\nفَقَالَ اَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْاَعْلٰى ۖ‏(24)\nFAQAALA ANAA RABBUKUMU A-A’LAA.\nAnd said ‘‘I am your Lord, the most High!\nفَاَخَذَهُ اللّٰهُ نَڪَالَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَالْاُوْلٰى ؕ‏(25)\nFAAKHAZAHU LAAHO NAALA AAKHERATE WAL OOLAA.\nSo seized him God, with the chastisement in the hereafter, and the life before (it)\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰىؕ‏(26)\nINNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAE’EBRATAN LEMAN YYAKHSHAA.\nVerily in this there is a lesson unto him who feareth (God).\nءَاَنْتُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمِ السَّمَآءُ‌ ؕ بَنٰٮهَا‏(27)\nA-ANTUM ASHADDO KHALQAN AMIL SAMAAA-O BANAAHAA.\nAre ye the harder to be created, or the heaven which built He?\nرَفَعَ سَمْكَهَا فَسَوَّٮهَا ۙ‏(28)\nRAFAA’A SAMKAHAA FASAWHAA.\nRaised He its heights and established it\nوَ اَغْطَشَ لَيْلَهَا وَاَخْرَجَ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(29)\nWA AAGHTASHA LAYLAHAA WA AKHRAJAL ZUHAAHAA.\nAnd He darkened its night, and brought forth its noon light\nوَالْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ دَحٰٮهَا ؕ‏(30)\nWAL ARZA BA’DA ZAALEKA DAHAAHAA.\nAnd the earth, afterwards he stretched forth\nاَخْرَجَ مِنْهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرْعٰٮهَا‏(31)\nAKHRAJAL MINHAA MAAAHAA WAMARA’AAHAA.\nHe brought forth from it, its waters and its pasteurage\nوَالْجِبَالَ اَرْسٰٮهَا ۙ‏(32)\nWA JEBAALA AARSAAHAA.\nAnd the mountains, He set them firm\nمَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(33)\nMATAA-A’M LAKUM WA LE-ANA’AMEKUM.\nA provision for you and your cattle\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الطَّآمَّةُ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(34)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-ATIS AT-TAAMMATU KUBRAA.\nWhen cometh the Great Calamity.\nيَوْمَ يَتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(35)\nYAWMA YATAZAKKARU INSAANO MAA SA-A’A.\nThe day when man shall recollect (all) that he strove for\nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِمَنْ يَّرٰى‏(36)\nWABURREZATE EZAL JAHEEMO LEMAN-Y YYARAA.\nAnd the hell shall be displayed unto him who seeth\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ طَغٰىۙ‏(37)\nFA-AMMAA MAN TAGHAA.\nThen, as for him who hath transgressed the bounds\nوَاٰثَرَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ۙ‏(38)\nWAASARA HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nAnd preferreth the life of this world\nفَاِنَّ الْجَحِيْمَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(39)\nFA-INNAL JAHEEM HEYA AL-MAAWAA.\nThen, verily, Hell, that shall be his abode\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ وَ نَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوٰىۙ‏(40)\nWA AMMAA MAN KHAAFA MAQAAMA RABBEHI WA NAHAA AN-NAFSA A’NIL AL-HAWAA.\nAnd as for him who feareth the standing of his Lord, and forbiddeth (his) self from (following) his inclinations\nفَاِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(41)\nFA-INNAL JANNATA HEYA AL-MAAWAA.\nThen, verily, the Garden (of Paradise), that shall be his abode\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ‏(42)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AS-SAAA’ATE AYYAANA MURSAAHAA.\nThey ask thee of ‘the Hour’ whereto (is) anchorage?\nفِيْمَ اَنْتَ مِنْ ذِكْرٰٮهَاؕ‏(43)\nFEEMA ANTA MIN ZEKRAAHAA.\nWherein art thou of its notion?\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ مُنْتَهٰٮهَاؕ‏(44)\nELAA RABBEKA MUNTAHAAHAA.\nUnto thy Lord (alone) is its termination!\nاِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰٮهَاؕ‏(45)\nINNAMAA ANTA MUNZERU MAN YYAKHSHAAHAA.\nThou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) art only a Warner unto him who feareth it\nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(46)\nKA-ANNAHUM YAWMA YARAWNAHAA LAM YALBASOOA ILLAA A’ASHEETAN AW ZUHAAHAA.\nIt shall seem unto them, on the day when they see it, as though they tarried not in (their graves) but a (single) evening, or the following morning",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naazea’at (Those Who Pull Out)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 42 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of entities in the Heavens."
